      "page_title": "Static vs Dynamic",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Vec<Box<dyn T>>` also pays one extra indirection per element.",
            "Static binary grows with (types x generic functions).",
            "Dynamic emits one vtable per type and one function body."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Build & Design"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "Static",
            "Dynamic"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "compile time",
              "slower",
              "faster"
            ],
            [
              "heterogeneity",
              "one type each",
              "mixed in one Vec"
            ],
            [
              "expressiveness",
              "generics, `Self`",
              "object safety only"
            ],
            [
              "error timing",
              "compile time",
              "downcast `None`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Static supports generic methods, `Self` returns, free associated types.",
            "`dyn` forces associated types to be spelled: `dyn Iterator<Item = u32>`.",
            "Static erases nothing, so misuse fails in full detail up front."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "API Stability",
          "text": "Adding a generic parameter is a breaking change to every caller signature. `dyn` keeps signatures fixed and localizes the churn inside your crate."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Choosing"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
