        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hybrid Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "pub fn log<W: Write>(w: &mut W) {",
            "  log_dyn(w)   // erase immediately",
            "}",
            "fn log_dyn(w: &mut dyn Write) {}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Caller ergonomics of generics, one code copy in the binary.",
            "Mirror image of the outlining trick from static dispatch.",
            "Public generic shim, private erased core."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Benchmark First",
          "text": "`dyn` overhead is usually invisible next to an allocation, an I/O wait, or a cache miss. Reach for it freely outside measured hot paths."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
